  "summary": "Traditional Māori fish hook pendants made from bone, stone, or wood, symbolizing prosperity, safe travel, and abundance.",
  "description": "Characterized by distinctive curved hook shape with intricate carving and often inlaid with paua shell, representing the importance of fishing to Māori culture and symbolizing abundance, strength, and determination. Developed as both practical fishing tools and prestigious ceremonial objects, with different designs representing specific tribes, families, and achievements.",
